1
00:00:01,125 --> 00:00:03,541
[moaning]

2
00:00:05,916 --> 00:00:07,000
[gasping]

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:08,708
-[playing unearthly tone]
-[Ras] What is that?

4
00:00:08,708 --> 00:00:11,541
Or... who is that?

5
00:00:12,583 --> 00:00:13,583
[playing unearthly tone]

6
00:00:13,583 --> 00:00:14,666
[Arin] Kur?

7
00:00:14,666 --> 00:00:17,208
I thought Thunderfang
ate all the Forbidden Five,

8
00:00:17,208 --> 00:00:18,208
or something.

9
00:00:18,208 --> 00:00:19,416
Are we sure he didn't?

10
00:00:19,416 --> 00:00:23,000
Kur looks... not amazing.

11
00:00:24,208 --> 00:00:25,708
They're back!

12
00:00:25,708 --> 00:00:27,458
[Sora] "They"?

13
00:00:30,708 --> 00:00:31,666
[spectral shrieking]

14
00:00:31,666 --> 00:00:32,875
[screaming]

15
00:00:33,958 --> 00:00:35,458
[screaming]

16
00:00:37,750 --> 00:00:38,791
[screaming]

17
00:00:39,583 --> 00:00:41,416
[spectral shrieking]

18
00:00:41,416 --> 00:00:42,958
It's an attack!

19
00:00:42,958 --> 00:00:43,833
By what?

20
00:00:43,833 --> 00:00:45,416
I don't see anything!

21
00:00:45,416 --> 00:00:48,000
I told you, they're invisible!

22
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:50,583
We must push them back somehow!

23
00:00:50,583 --> 00:00:53,625
[grunting with effort]

24
00:00:53,625 --> 00:00:55,291
Kind of hard
to smack someone in the face

25
00:00:55,291 --> 00:00:57,000
when you can't see their face!

26
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:58,625
[grunting with effort]

27
00:00:58,625 --> 00:01:00,041
[spectral shrieking]

28
00:01:00,041 --> 00:01:02,750
This is just like last night!

29
00:01:02,750 --> 00:01:05,291
I've never seen
anything like this before.

30
00:01:06,666 --> 00:01:09,416
Pun not intended!
Now is not the time for jokes!

31
00:01:09,416 --> 00:01:10,458
Wait!

32
00:01:10,458 --> 00:01:12,625
I<i> have </i>seen something
like this before!

33
00:01:14,166 --> 00:01:16,208
They're Dragonians?

34
00:01:16,208 --> 00:01:18,083
Invisible Dragonians?

35
00:01:18,083 --> 00:01:19,166
They look like
the Soul Suckers

36
00:01:19,166 --> 00:01:21,208
from the Spectral Lands!

37
00:01:21,208 --> 00:01:23,166
[crowd screaming in terror]

38
00:01:23,166 --> 00:01:25,916
[playing unearthly tone]

39
00:01:27,208 --> 00:01:30,041
They're draining their lives
into that weird instrument!

40
00:01:30,041 --> 00:01:32,916
[panicked screaming]

41
00:01:36,833 --> 00:01:38,916
When I say duck, duck!

42
00:01:38,916 --> 00:01:40,791
My blade's
made of Prismatic Steel!

43
00:01:40,791 --> 00:01:42,333
It should stop them!

44
00:01:42,333 --> 00:01:43,458
[Sora] Arin?

45
00:01:43,458 --> 00:01:45,125
When for the ducking?

46
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:47,083
[spectral shrieking]

47
00:01:48,875 --> 00:01:50,208
Now!

48
00:01:52,416 --> 00:01:54,458
Oh, that's bad!

49
00:01:54,458 --> 00:01:57,125
Not only did my blade
not destroy them,

50
00:01:57,125 --> 00:01:59,625
these things can break
prismatic steel!

51
00:02:01,500 --> 00:02:04,791
♪ Lost in the unknown ♪

52
00:02:04,791 --> 00:02:07,708
♪ Together we will rise ♪

53
00:02:07,708 --> 00:02:11,166
♪ We fight ♪

54
00:02:11,166 --> 00:02:14,208
♪ Be a ninja for what's right ♪

55
00:02:15,541 --> 00:02:16,541
[thunderclap]

56
00:02:17,541 --> 00:02:19,291
[♪♪♪]

57
00:02:27,041 --> 00:02:29,416
[Jay] When we get there,
let me do all the talking.

58
00:02:29,416 --> 00:02:32,500
I don't need so-called Ninja
ruining my flow.

59
00:02:32,500 --> 00:02:33,500
-Ah!
-Whoa!

60
00:02:35,583 --> 00:02:37,291
[yelping and groaning]

61
00:02:38,708 --> 00:02:40,250
Did we hit something?

62
00:02:40,250 --> 00:02:41,125
[groaning] No...

63
00:02:41,125 --> 00:02:41,958
[cackling]

64
00:02:43,583 --> 00:02:45,333
-Whoa!
-[yelping]

65
00:02:45,333 --> 00:02:47,250
...just Wyldfyre's driving.

66
00:02:47,250 --> 00:02:49,333
Weren't you supposed to
practice flying this thing

67
00:02:49,333 --> 00:02:50,541
before we left?

68
00:02:50,541 --> 00:02:52,625
Aw, me, me, me, me!

69
00:02:52,625 --> 00:02:54,875
Weren't you supposed
to not be so judgy

70
00:02:54,875 --> 00:02:56,333
about my driving?

71
00:02:56,333 --> 00:02:57,875
I'm the captain now!

72
00:02:57,875 --> 00:03:00,541
My ship, my rules!

73
00:03:02,416 --> 00:03:03,666
[all groaning]

74
00:03:03,666 --> 00:03:06,166
[Nya] Can you just
keep your eyes on the... sky?

75
00:03:06,166 --> 00:03:09,666
Okay! How about
your face to the sky?!

76
00:03:09,666 --> 00:03:11,166
[groaning]

77
00:03:12,625 --> 00:03:15,750
[whistling nonchalantly]

78
00:03:15,750 --> 00:03:18,166
I've been
to the Administration before.

79
00:03:18,166 --> 00:03:20,666
Fine by me if you want to do
all the talking, Jay.

80
00:03:20,666 --> 00:03:23,791
They'll probably fine me
for not having a talking permit.

81
00:03:23,791 --> 00:03:25,583
How did you ending up
working there, anyway?

82
00:03:25,583 --> 00:03:27,083
It's a long story...

83
00:03:28,333 --> 00:03:30,208
Or a short story. Who knows?

84
00:03:30,208 --> 00:03:32,583
I have zero memory of anything
before the Merge!

85
00:03:32,583 --> 00:03:34,083
We've told you
what your life was like

86
00:03:34,083 --> 00:03:35,208
before the Merge.

87
00:03:35,208 --> 00:03:37,458
Yeah.
So did the Administration.

88
00:03:37,458 --> 00:03:38,916
So did Ras.

89
00:03:38,916 --> 00:03:41,583
I now know
not to believe any of you.

90
00:03:41,583 --> 00:03:43,041
But I do know this--

91
00:03:43,041 --> 00:03:44,416
my first memories,

92
00:03:44,416 --> 00:03:47,666
I found myself alone
in the Land of Madness.

93
00:03:47,666 --> 00:03:49,458
Didn't even know my name.

94
00:03:49,458 --> 00:03:51,083
Then I spotted
some nice young people

95
00:03:51,083 --> 00:03:52,208
in business suits,

96
00:03:52,208 --> 00:03:54,375
and I just had a feeling
I could trust them.

97
00:03:54,375 --> 00:03:55,958
Because
they were wearing suits?

98
00:03:55,958 --> 00:03:56,958
Yeah!

99
00:03:56,958 --> 00:03:58,041
So I went up to them,

100
00:03:58,041 --> 00:04:00,125
and it turns out
they were looking for me.

101
00:04:00,125 --> 00:04:01,916
They told me
my name was Jay Walker,

102
00:04:01,916 --> 00:04:04,166
and that I was
an Agent of the Administration,

103
00:04:04,166 --> 00:04:05,583
just like them.

104
00:04:05,583 --> 00:04:07,083
How'd they know your name?

105
00:04:07,083 --> 00:04:09,291
How does the Administration
know anything?

106
00:04:09,291 --> 00:04:11,333
They said I'd worked there
my whole life,

107
00:04:11,333 --> 00:04:13,000
and had to get back to my job

108
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:15,333
managing
the Realm Reassignment Office.

109
00:04:15,333 --> 00:04:17,791
And you just... believed them?

110
00:04:17,791 --> 00:04:19,125
Suits, greenie.

111
00:04:19,125 --> 00:04:20,291
<i>Suits.</i>

112
00:04:22,458 --> 00:04:24,000
<i>Turns out I was a natural,</i>

113
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:26,083
<i>so it made sense</i>
<i>that's who I really was.</i>

114
00:04:29,250 --> 00:04:31,833
<i>[Nya] So these Suits</i>
<i>claimed to know you?</i>

115
00:04:34,625 --> 00:04:36,291
Their boss did.

116
00:04:36,291 --> 00:04:38,375
Apparently the Administrator
sent them a message

117
00:04:38,375 --> 00:04:39,458
to go and get me.

118
00:04:39,458 --> 00:04:41,375
[yelping]

119
00:04:44,083 --> 00:04:45,625
Who's the Administrator?

120
00:04:45,625 --> 00:04:46,625
No clue.

121
00:04:46,625 --> 00:04:47,750
No one I talked to

122
00:04:47,750 --> 00:04:49,916
had ever actually seen him,

123
00:04:49,916 --> 00:04:53,250
or her, or them, or it?

124
00:04:53,250 --> 00:04:54,666
Sounds creepy.

125
00:04:54,666 --> 00:04:56,916
So, what did you
actually do there?

126
00:04:56,916 --> 00:04:58,708
<i>[Jay, exasperatedly]</i>
<i>Ugh! Realm Reassignment!</i>

127
00:04:58,708 --> 00:05:00,333
<i>You know this!</i>

128
00:05:00,333 --> 00:05:02,291
<i>People they'd find</i>
<i>in empty space bubbles</i>

129
00:05:02,291 --> 00:05:03,708
<i>after the Merge.</i>

130
00:05:03,708 --> 00:05:05,125
<i>My job was to send them back</i>

131
00:05:05,125 --> 00:05:06,833
<i>to wherever</i>
<i>I thought they came from.</i>

132
00:05:06,833 --> 00:05:08,791
<i>[Lloyd] Where you thought</i>
<i>they came from?</i>

133
00:05:08,791 --> 00:05:12,083
<i>You, who has no memory</i>
<i>of anything or anywhere</i>

134
00:05:12,083 --> 00:05:13,291
<i>from before the Merge?</i>

135
00:05:13,291 --> 00:05:14,166
Aah!

136
00:05:16,500 --> 00:05:17,958
I was working with

137
00:05:17,958 --> 00:05:20,041
the best information
I could get,

138
00:05:20,041 --> 00:05:22,208
and sure, there might have been
a few mix-ups,

139
00:05:22,208 --> 00:05:23,416
but there's no proof of that,

140
00:05:23,416 --> 00:05:24,750
and if there was proof,

141
00:05:24,750 --> 00:05:26,541
it would have been shredded
and/or burned.

142
00:05:26,541 --> 00:05:27,541
Aah!

143
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:31,125
"Just a few mix-ups"?

144
00:05:31,125 --> 00:05:34,000
You're famously terrible
at guessing games.

145
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:34,875
Hey!

146
00:05:34,875 --> 00:05:35,750
No lie.

147
00:05:35,750 --> 00:05:37,083
You tank every Charades team

148
00:05:37,083 --> 00:05:38,458
you've ever been on.

149
00:05:38,458 --> 00:05:41,583
You expect me to believe
I ever played Charades?

150
00:05:41,583 --> 00:05:44,208
I don't even know
what Charades is!

151
00:05:44,208 --> 00:05:46,625
Yet you remember
Arin's parents?

152
00:05:46,625 --> 00:05:48,416
Of course. Jenny and Barry.

153
00:05:48,416 --> 00:05:51,166
I had to enter reassignment logs
every night in triplicate,

154
00:05:51,166 --> 00:05:53,458
then in the weekly reports,
then the monthly reports,

155
00:05:53,458 --> 00:05:54,875
plus corporate memos.

156
00:05:54,875 --> 00:05:56,666
So that's how you know
where they are now?

157
00:05:56,666 --> 00:05:57,916
Yeah, where I sent them.

158
00:05:57,916 --> 00:05:59,250
The Land of Lee.

159
00:05:59,250 --> 00:06:01,750
[Wyldfyre] Then why aren't we
flying straight there

160
00:06:01,750 --> 00:06:05,208
instead of wasting our time
at the Administration?

161
00:06:05,208 --> 00:06:07,041
[all yelping] Whoa!

162
00:06:07,041 --> 00:06:08,000
-Aah!
-Whoa!

163
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:09,208
[grunting]

164
00:06:09,208 --> 00:06:11,666
You can get to the location
by air or boat,

165
00:06:11,666 --> 00:06:14,458
but the only way to get into
the real Land of Lee

166
00:06:14,458 --> 00:06:16,666
is through
the Realm Reassignment Area.

167
00:06:16,666 --> 00:06:17,958
It won't make any sense

168
00:06:17,958 --> 00:06:19,583
until you experience it
for yourselves.

169
00:06:19,583 --> 00:06:22,375
[shuddering] Oh...
sounds dangerous.

170
00:06:22,375 --> 00:06:23,750
Now I'm excited.

171
00:06:23,750 --> 00:06:25,166
And we can trust you?

172
00:06:25,166 --> 00:06:27,708
You<i> did </i>shatter your goodness.

173
00:06:27,708 --> 00:06:29,458
You have no reason to trust me,

174
00:06:29,458 --> 00:06:31,666
but you don't have a choice,
do you?

175
00:06:31,666 --> 00:06:32,916
H'yah!

176
00:06:32,916 --> 00:06:33,958
Sold!

177
00:06:33,958 --> 00:06:35,666
Let's go!

178
00:06:35,666 --> 00:06:36,958
[yelping]

179
00:06:36,958 --> 00:06:38,875
But... what's with the cake?

180
00:06:38,875 --> 00:06:41,500
Let's just hope
we don't have to use it.

181
00:06:43,166 --> 00:06:45,458
[♪♪♪]

182
00:06:45,458 --> 00:06:48,125
-Whoa!
-[yelping]

183
00:06:48,125 --> 00:06:49,333
[spectral shrieking]

184
00:06:51,291 --> 00:06:52,250
[shrieking]

185
00:06:52,250 --> 00:06:54,833
This is not our battle!

186
00:06:54,833 --> 00:06:56,250
These people need our help!

187
00:06:56,250 --> 00:06:58,625
The Pontifex Magicus
has been hollowed,

188
00:06:58,625 --> 00:07:00,541
and is of no use to me anymore.

189
00:07:00,541 --> 00:07:01,708
[Sora] We're not leaving!

190
00:07:01,708 --> 00:07:03,208
[spectral shrieking]

191
00:07:06,833 --> 00:07:08,208
[shrieking]

192
00:07:08,208 --> 00:07:09,416
[Arin] Duck!

193
00:07:09,416 --> 00:07:10,458
H'yah!

194
00:07:14,208 --> 00:07:15,583
[gasping]

195
00:07:18,791 --> 00:07:21,500
Can't say I'm into fighting
with a stubby blade.

196
00:07:21,500 --> 00:07:22,708
Where's the other half?

197
00:07:22,708 --> 00:07:24,500
What, you have some glue?

198
00:07:27,375 --> 00:07:28,416
[gasping]

199
00:07:37,458 --> 00:07:39,083
Can you light this up?

200
00:07:39,083 --> 00:07:40,583
A brighter color?

201
00:07:40,583 --> 00:07:43,083
I think that might be
a bit gaudy for the--

202
00:07:43,083 --> 00:07:45,125
No, illuminate it!

203
00:07:45,125 --> 00:07:46,916
Oh, light it up.

204
00:07:46,916 --> 00:07:48,708
Why didn't you say so?

205
00:07:50,708 --> 00:07:53,583
Could you use a coconut?

206
00:07:53,583 --> 00:07:55,916
No! I need light!

207
00:07:55,916 --> 00:07:56,916
Just asking.

208
00:07:56,916 --> 00:07:59,250
Some people like coconuts.

209
00:07:59,250 --> 00:08:00,625
I guess not you.

210
00:08:02,541 --> 00:08:04,208
[spectral shrieking]

211
00:08:04,208 --> 00:08:05,833
[Sora] Wow.

212
00:08:05,833 --> 00:08:09,208
There are way more
of these things than I realized.

213
00:08:09,208 --> 00:08:10,666
[Arin] Come on! This way!

214
00:08:10,666 --> 00:08:12,083
[Ras] We must leave!

215
00:08:12,083 --> 00:08:15,041
The only reason we came here
was to find the Underworld.

216
00:08:15,041 --> 00:08:17,458
Oh, the Underworld.
I know exactly where that is.

217
00:08:17,458 --> 00:08:19,333
Well, not exactly, but I know
exactly where my map is,

218
00:08:19,333 --> 00:08:20,333
and that would tell me exactly.

219
00:08:20,333 --> 00:08:21,333
[Ras] Where?

220
00:08:21,333 --> 00:08:22,333
[screaming]

221
00:08:22,333 --> 00:08:24,250
Ninja! Protect this woman!

222
00:08:24,250 --> 00:08:26,000
She can help us on our quest.

223
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:28,208
[Sorceress]
I can take care of myself!

224
00:08:30,083 --> 00:08:31,458
Anchors away!

225
00:08:35,333 --> 00:08:36,458
[yelping and wailing]

226
00:08:38,625 --> 00:08:40,250
[groaning]

227
00:08:40,250 --> 00:08:41,333
Everyone alive?

228
00:08:41,333 --> 00:08:42,750
Not sure.

229
00:08:50,041 --> 00:08:51,583
I've never seen
the Administration

230
00:08:51,583 --> 00:08:53,541
from the outside.

231
00:08:53,541 --> 00:08:54,791
It's so...

232
00:08:54,791 --> 00:08:55,958
boring.

233
00:08:55,958 --> 00:08:57,791
[Nya]
I'm looking directly at it

234
00:08:57,791 --> 00:09:00,083
and already forgot
everything about it.

235
00:09:01,791 --> 00:09:03,583
So, how are we sneaking in?

236
00:09:03,583 --> 00:09:05,041
Air vent? Basement?

237
00:09:05,041 --> 00:09:08,041
Blast a giant hole? Please?

238
00:09:08,041 --> 00:09:09,166
My instinct is a full attack,

239
00:09:09,166 --> 00:09:10,208
swords slicing,

240
00:09:10,208 --> 00:09:11,750
taking out any and every Agent

241
00:09:11,750 --> 00:09:13,875
that dares stand up to us.

242
00:09:13,875 --> 00:09:16,416
Show them what true power is...

243
00:09:16,416 --> 00:09:17,333
[chuckling]

244
00:09:17,333 --> 00:09:19,041
...but there's too many of them,

245
00:09:19,041 --> 00:09:20,791
and that plan could fail.

246
00:09:20,791 --> 00:09:23,708
And that's not
how Ninja handle things.

247
00:09:23,708 --> 00:09:26,458
You really did shatter
your goodness, didn't you?

248
00:09:26,458 --> 00:09:28,625
It's cute you think
I had goodness to shatter.

249
00:09:29,666 --> 00:09:32,041
Nope, straight-on attack
won't work,

250
00:09:32,041 --> 00:09:34,583
so I got something better.

251
00:09:35,625 --> 00:09:36,916
[♪♪♪]

252
00:09:36,916 --> 00:09:39,041
Suits, am I right?

253
00:09:39,041 --> 00:09:40,333
Now, watch this.

254
00:09:44,500 --> 00:09:45,625
[beeping]

255
00:09:53,875 --> 00:09:54,708
Halt!

256
00:09:54,708 --> 00:09:56,708
Allen! Underwood!

257
00:09:56,708 --> 00:09:57,833
What's shakin'?

258
00:09:57,833 --> 00:10:01,208
A little informal
for a morning greeting,

259
00:10:01,208 --> 00:10:03,958
but it is casual Friday,

260
00:10:03,958 --> 00:10:05,250
so I'll allow it.

261
00:10:05,250 --> 00:10:08,166
Returning from sabbatical,
Agent Jay Walker?

262
00:10:08,166 --> 00:10:09,583
Yep, and since today

263
00:10:09,583 --> 00:10:12,041
is "Bring your Ninja Warrior
Friends To Work Day,"

264
00:10:12,041 --> 00:10:13,541
I have companions.

265
00:10:13,541 --> 00:10:14,708
Heading to Guest Services

266
00:10:14,708 --> 00:10:17,458
to fill out their paperwork
and get temporary badges.

267
00:10:17,458 --> 00:10:18,666
Hmm...

268
00:10:18,666 --> 00:10:20,916
"Bring Your Ninja Warrior
Friends To Work Day"

269
00:10:20,916 --> 00:10:22,666
was last week.

270
00:10:22,666 --> 00:10:23,750
[charging weapons]

271
00:10:23,750 --> 00:10:25,708
[Nya] That escalated quickly.

272
00:10:25,708 --> 00:10:29,875
Uh, we must've just got
the B-Y-N... W-F...

273
00:10:29,875 --> 00:10:32,750
T-W day wrong?

274
00:10:32,750 --> 00:10:35,208
That's not
your most egregious offense,

275
00:10:35,208 --> 00:10:36,333
Agent Walker.

276
00:10:36,333 --> 00:10:39,375
you have long been
on our Most Wanted List

277
00:10:39,375 --> 00:10:41,125
for abandoning your post!

278
00:10:42,958 --> 00:10:44,333
[spectral shrieking]

279
00:10:44,333 --> 00:10:45,166
[blasting]

280
00:10:47,250 --> 00:10:49,708
[spectral shrieking]

281
00:10:50,416 --> 00:10:51,291
Yaah!

282
00:10:54,916 --> 00:10:56,166
[shrieking]

283
00:10:58,166 --> 00:10:59,375
[shrieking]

284
00:11:00,083 --> 00:11:01,500
Whoa!

285
00:11:01,500 --> 00:11:02,583
[grunting]

286
00:11:03,458 --> 00:11:05,291
[shrieking]

287
00:11:05,291 --> 00:11:07,000
I'm okay!

288
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:07,916
Yuck!

289
00:11:08,916 --> 00:11:10,500
We must leave!

290
00:11:10,500 --> 00:11:12,750
It's the only way
to keep you truly safe!

291
00:11:12,750 --> 00:11:14,125
Forget it, kitten!

292
00:11:14,125 --> 00:11:15,625
I'm going to protect
this village

293
00:11:15,625 --> 00:11:17,625
with my last puff of magic,
if I must!

294
00:11:17,625 --> 00:11:18,666
[shrieking]

295
00:11:20,500 --> 00:11:21,666
[gasping in horror]

296
00:11:23,958 --> 00:11:24,958
[playing unearthly tone]

297
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:33,333
[spectral shrieking]

298
00:11:36,750 --> 00:11:37,875
[playing unearthly tone]

299
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:40,625
[Arin] What's happening?

300
00:11:40,625 --> 00:11:41,708
[Sora] It's morning.

301
00:11:41,708 --> 00:11:43,833
They must not be able
to stand the sun!

302
00:11:43,833 --> 00:11:45,083
[Arin] I don't understand.

303
00:11:45,083 --> 00:11:48,375
It's like the Spectral Lands
spread into this town,

304
00:11:48,375 --> 00:11:50,541
but only have power at night.

305
00:11:50,541 --> 00:11:52,333
Can these people be cured?

306
00:11:52,333 --> 00:11:55,375
Do we need to hunt down Kur
and return their life-forces?

307
00:11:55,375 --> 00:11:57,041
[Ras] Forget them.

308
00:11:57,041 --> 00:12:00,375
Our goal is to forge
Source Dragon icons,

309
00:12:00,375 --> 00:12:02,916
and because of your choices,
we failed.

310
00:12:02,916 --> 00:12:04,291
Hey, that's not our fault.

311
00:12:04,291 --> 00:12:06,375
[Ras] It is your fault.

312
00:12:06,375 --> 00:12:08,916
Yours and the Sorceress's
selfishness.

313
00:12:08,916 --> 00:12:10,291
Without her help,

314
00:12:10,291 --> 00:12:13,291
we are forced to find
another way to the Underworld!

315
00:12:13,291 --> 00:12:15,375
If that's even possible.

316
00:12:17,833 --> 00:12:19,041
Cole and Zane said

317
00:12:19,041 --> 00:12:21,250
she lives in the Monastery
that appeared here.

318
00:12:21,250 --> 00:12:23,458
Maybe if we take her back home,

319
00:12:23,458 --> 00:12:25,916
we can help her get less...
hollowed out,

320
00:12:25,916 --> 00:12:27,791
and find her map
to the Underworld.

321
00:12:27,791 --> 00:12:30,000
Sora, that's a great idea!

322
00:12:31,291 --> 00:12:32,291
[Ras growling]

323
00:12:33,375 --> 00:12:36,041
Let us find this Monastery.

324
00:12:36,041 --> 00:12:39,083
[Lloyd] I can't believe
you got us stuck in here.

325
00:12:39,083 --> 00:12:41,125
What kind of plan was that?

326
00:12:41,125 --> 00:12:42,375
This is just like you.

327
00:12:42,375 --> 00:12:44,750
You always had the weirdest,
worst ideas,

328
00:12:44,750 --> 00:12:46,791
but usually
they were charming somehow.

329
00:12:46,791 --> 00:12:48,416
This one is just plain stupid.

330
00:12:48,416 --> 00:12:49,500
[Jay] Trust me.

331
00:12:49,500 --> 00:12:51,958
Everything is going
exactly as planned.

332
00:12:51,958 --> 00:12:53,875
Don't see how that's possible.

333
00:12:53,875 --> 00:12:55,666
I knew the moment
we entered the building,

334
00:12:55,666 --> 00:12:56,833
alarms would go off,

335
00:12:56,833 --> 00:12:59,250
'cause I left the company,
which no one ever does.

336
00:12:59,250 --> 00:13:00,500
Then we'd get sent here,

337
00:13:00,500 --> 00:13:02,208
deep into the inner workings,

338
00:13:02,208 --> 00:13:03,916
exactly where we need to be.

339
00:13:03,916 --> 00:13:05,333
In a cell with no escape?

340
00:13:05,333 --> 00:13:06,958
Yeah! It's perfect,

341
00:13:06,958 --> 00:13:08,625
'cause now
the Administration thinks

342
00:13:08,625 --> 00:13:11,083
they have us
under their control.

343
00:13:11,083 --> 00:13:14,208
Now all we have to do
is escape.

344
00:13:14,208 --> 00:13:15,166
Hey!

345
00:13:15,166 --> 00:13:16,791
Agent Etha!

346
00:13:16,791 --> 00:13:19,458
Yes, I'm talking to you!

347
00:13:19,458 --> 00:13:22,416
I know you don't get
much company in here...

348
00:13:22,416 --> 00:13:23,500
[chuckling]

349
00:13:23,500 --> 00:13:25,625
So, Agent Underwood told me

350
00:13:25,625 --> 00:13:26,750
you were really into

351
00:13:26,750 --> 00:13:29,583
Merlopian Dance Rituals
and Celebrations!

352
00:13:29,583 --> 00:13:32,333
Any interest in telling us
more about that?

353
00:13:32,333 --> 00:13:36,291
I've been waiting for someone
to ask me that my whole life!

354
00:13:36,291 --> 00:13:38,541
Dance ethnography

355
00:13:38,541 --> 00:13:40,833
is a really
fascinating subject...

356
00:13:40,833 --> 00:13:43,500
...and they showered them
with exotic flowers...

357
00:13:43,500 --> 00:13:46,208
...the town would elect
a sacrifice, and...

358
00:13:46,208 --> 00:13:48,250
...the lights would fade up,

359
00:13:48,250 --> 00:13:50,041
and the lead dancer
would descend

360
00:13:50,041 --> 00:13:52,083
with a fan and a lantern...

361
00:13:52,083 --> 00:13:54,416
[whispering]
...and the magical eel...

362
00:13:54,416 --> 00:13:55,666
[giggling excitedly]

363
00:13:55,666 --> 00:13:57,416
Y-You sure I'm not boring you?

364
00:13:57,416 --> 00:13:58,583
Anyway,

365
00:13:58,583 --> 00:14:02,000
the audience threw gummy candy
on the stage!

366
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:04,000
Shall I demonstrate?

367
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:05,458
Ha! [giggling]

368
00:14:05,458 --> 00:14:07,416
Ta-da!

369
00:14:07,416 --> 00:14:09,250
[whispering] Eat the candy...

370
00:14:10,208 --> 00:14:12,833
That was informative, Etha,

371
00:14:12,833 --> 00:14:15,458
and, uh, doesn't
their sacred winter dance

372
00:14:15,458 --> 00:14:18,000
involve a blindfold?

373
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:20,500
I can't believe you know that!

374
00:14:20,500 --> 00:14:23,958
And I just so happen to have
my dance blindfold with me

375
00:14:23,958 --> 00:14:26,375
for exactly
this potential scenario!

376
00:14:26,375 --> 00:14:27,958
[singing] ♪ Hey-ya ♪

377
00:14:27,958 --> 00:14:30,916
♪ Ya-ya-ya-ya ♪

378
00:14:30,916 --> 00:14:33,125
[snorting and vocalizing]

379
00:14:33,125 --> 00:14:34,791
♪ H'yah-ya-ya ♪

380
00:14:34,791 --> 00:14:37,875
I trust you're still there
and enjoying this silently!

381
00:14:37,875 --> 00:14:40,500
She's a fantastic dancer!

382
00:14:40,500 --> 00:14:41,500
[Jay] Be right back.

383
00:14:41,500 --> 00:14:42,875
I need something
from the locker room.

384
00:14:42,875 --> 00:14:44,791
What could you need
from a locker room?

385
00:14:44,791 --> 00:14:47,625
It's where Agent Leopold
keeps his gym shorts.

386
00:14:47,625 --> 00:14:49,625
I'm going to need
more information.

387
00:14:49,625 --> 00:14:51,916
He never washes them.

388
00:14:57,208 --> 00:14:58,833
[groaning and gagging] Oh!

389
00:14:58,833 --> 00:15:00,166
Oh, man!

390
00:15:02,333 --> 00:15:03,708
[gagging] Yuck!

391
00:15:03,708 --> 00:15:05,666
[pneumatic tube hissing]

392
00:15:08,208 --> 00:15:09,166
[sniffing]

393
00:15:09,166 --> 00:15:12,500
Ugh! What is that?

394
00:15:12,500 --> 00:15:13,625
[groaning]

395
00:15:13,625 --> 00:15:15,708
That smells like Agent Leopold!

396
00:15:15,708 --> 00:15:17,500
[gasping for air]

397
00:15:17,500 --> 00:15:18,541
[groaning and gagging]

398
00:15:18,541 --> 00:15:19,750
Call the Detox Crew!

399
00:15:19,750 --> 00:15:21,416
[all groaning]

400
00:15:22,500 --> 00:15:24,750
[humming Agent Etha's
dance music]

401
00:15:24,750 --> 00:15:27,083
Ooh, I should learn
Merlopian dances!

402
00:15:28,708 --> 00:15:31,166
[alert blaring]

403
00:15:31,166 --> 00:15:32,208
It wasn't me.

404
00:15:32,208 --> 00:15:33,916
Why did you come along?

405
00:15:33,916 --> 00:15:35,666
All you do is mess things up!

406
00:15:35,666 --> 00:15:36,833
You can't drive right,

407
00:15:36,833 --> 00:15:38,875
you dance into alarms, you--

408
00:15:38,875 --> 00:15:40,333
[gasping] More Ninja?

409
00:15:40,333 --> 00:15:44,208
When it's not "Bring your Ninja
Warrior Friends To Work Day"?

410
00:15:44,208 --> 00:15:45,750
Those are the same Ninja!

411
00:15:45,750 --> 00:15:47,166
And Jay Walker!

412
00:15:47,166 --> 00:15:48,708
They flew the coop!

413
00:15:48,708 --> 00:15:49,875
[weapons charging]

414
00:15:49,875 --> 00:15:52,500
Curse you, Agent Etha!

415
00:15:52,500 --> 00:15:53,500
[coughing]

416
00:15:55,541 --> 00:15:57,291
[gagging] Oh, the stench!

417
00:15:57,291 --> 00:16:00,125
It's... [gagging]
...in my lungs!

418
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:07,958
[moaning and mumbling]

419
00:16:07,958 --> 00:16:10,083
[Arin] I think the Sorceress
is coming to.

420
00:16:10,083 --> 00:16:12,333
She sees her home!

421
00:16:12,333 --> 00:16:14,000
[mumbling]

422
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:15,458
[Sora] Maybe
it'll get better inside?

423
00:16:18,166 --> 00:16:21,541
[alert tone chiming]

424
00:16:22,291 --> 00:16:24,000
[Ras grumbles]

425
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:25,208
Some kind of security.

426
00:16:25,208 --> 00:16:26,208
It shouldn't be a probl--

427
00:16:26,208 --> 00:16:27,041
[grunting]

428
00:16:27,041 --> 00:16:27,875
Ha ha ha!

429
00:16:27,875 --> 00:16:29,500
-Oof!
-Ha ha! Oof!

430
00:16:29,500 --> 00:16:30,500
[groaning]

431
00:16:30,500 --> 00:16:32,750
<i>I hope you enjoy my traps!</i>

432
00:16:32,750 --> 00:16:35,666
<i>That's what you get</i>
<i>for trying to break in,</i>

433
00:16:35,666 --> 00:16:36,833
<i>whoever you are.</i>

434
00:16:36,833 --> 00:16:39,041
<i>Predictable as always, Janet!</i>

435
00:16:42,416 --> 00:16:43,500
Who's Janet?

436
00:16:43,500 --> 00:16:45,291
[yelping and wailing]

437
00:16:45,291 --> 00:16:47,208
[grunting and struggling]

438
00:16:47,916 --> 00:16:50,333
[Jay] We're almost
to Realm Reassignment!

439
00:16:50,333 --> 00:16:51,375
We'll be safe as soon as--

440
00:16:52,250 --> 00:16:54,333
[weapons charging]

441
00:16:57,458 --> 00:16:59,541
Was this part of the plan?

442
00:16:59,541 --> 00:17:01,750
[sighing] I didn't want
to have to do this.

443
00:17:01,750 --> 00:17:02,958
Green guy...

444
00:17:04,375 --> 00:17:05,500
Cake me.

445
00:17:08,750 --> 00:17:09,750
Everybody!

446
00:17:09,750 --> 00:17:12,000
We've got an office birthday
today,

447
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:14,333
and you've all
got to sign this card!

448
00:17:14,333 --> 00:17:15,916
Ooh, a birthday!

449
00:17:15,916 --> 00:17:19,333
-Leave some space for me!
-Who didn't sign? Did you sign?

450
00:17:19,333 --> 00:17:22,583
[Nya] Hey, we need plates!
And napkins!

451
00:17:22,583 --> 00:17:24,083
Who's got plates and napkins?

452
00:17:24,083 --> 00:17:25,208
Forks? Are there forks?

453
00:17:25,208 --> 00:17:26,541
Whose birthday is it? Carl's?

454
00:17:26,541 --> 00:17:28,208
No, he just had his birthday!

455
00:17:28,208 --> 00:17:29,166
[Agents clamoring]

456
00:17:32,166 --> 00:17:35,375
Come on, we need new clothes
from Lost and Found!

457
00:17:36,625 --> 00:17:37,916
[Ras grumbles]

458
00:17:37,916 --> 00:17:38,916
Do something!

459
00:17:38,916 --> 00:17:40,666
Use your Elemental Powers!

460
00:17:41,958 --> 00:17:42,958
[grunting]

461
00:17:42,958 --> 00:17:45,333
There's no tech
in this monastery!

462
00:17:45,333 --> 00:17:48,541
[Sorceress mumbling]

463
00:17:48,541 --> 00:17:50,416
Wait a minute...

464
00:17:51,750 --> 00:17:53,250
[Sorceress protesting]

465
00:17:53,250 --> 00:17:54,958
What are you doing?

466
00:17:54,958 --> 00:17:56,000
Casting a spell!

467
00:17:56,000 --> 00:17:57,750
You don't know any spells!

468
00:17:57,750 --> 00:18:00,458
Nope, but maybe
we'll hit on something.

469
00:18:00,458 --> 00:18:02,041
[coughing]

470
00:18:03,750 --> 00:18:05,375
[wheezing] Not that.

471
00:18:06,333 --> 00:18:08,583
Feels like
we're getting closer?

472
00:18:08,583 --> 00:18:10,083
I'm not sure that's true.

473
00:18:10,083 --> 00:18:12,833
[Sorceress mumbling]

474
00:18:12,833 --> 00:18:14,416
This is getting us nowhere!

475
00:18:15,500 --> 00:18:18,458
No, but maybe these
could get us somewhere.

476
00:18:18,458 --> 00:18:19,625
We can hold onto these fish

477
00:18:19,625 --> 00:18:22,250
and pull ourselves out!

478
00:18:22,250 --> 00:18:23,250
[grunting]

479
00:18:23,250 --> 00:18:24,333
This now tops

480
00:18:24,333 --> 00:18:27,000
my "Weirdest Things
I've Ever Done" list.

481
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:28,250
[Ras grunting]

482
00:18:29,708 --> 00:18:31,166
[grunting with effort]

483
00:18:31,166 --> 00:18:32,166
Aah!

484
00:18:32,166 --> 00:18:33,375
Oof!

485
00:18:52,583 --> 00:18:53,458
A-ha!

486
00:18:55,125 --> 00:18:56,583
[Ras] The Underworld.

487
00:19:01,958 --> 00:19:03,041
[grunting awkwardly]

488
00:19:03,041 --> 00:19:04,208
Why?

489
00:19:04,208 --> 00:19:06,166
Told you,
the Land of Lee is weird,

490
00:19:06,166 --> 00:19:07,958
and you definitely
can't parade in there

491
00:19:07,958 --> 00:19:09,541
dressed like a Ninja.

492
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:17,666
[typing rapidly]

493
00:19:21,541 --> 00:19:23,458
Ha ha! Still got it.

494
00:19:23,458 --> 00:19:24,916
Oh, one more thing.

495
00:19:24,916 --> 00:19:25,958
For some reason,

496
00:19:25,958 --> 00:19:27,583
everyone who got lost
in the space bubbles

497
00:19:27,583 --> 00:19:28,666
were mostly a pair,

498
00:19:28,666 --> 00:19:30,666
like, siblings,
couples, whatever.

499
00:19:30,666 --> 00:19:32,375
We need fake stories like that.

500
00:19:32,375 --> 00:19:33,791
If we're going undercover,

501
00:19:33,791 --> 00:19:35,916
Wyldfyre, you and I
are brother and sister...

502
00:19:35,916 --> 00:19:36,916
Barf.

503
00:19:36,916 --> 00:19:39,333
...and Jay and Nya
are married.

504
00:19:39,333 --> 00:19:40,875
Gross, but okay.

505
00:19:40,875 --> 00:19:42,000
[typing rapidly]

506
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:43,916
Everybody ready?

507
00:19:43,916 --> 00:19:45,083
[portal powering up]

508
00:19:48,333 --> 00:19:50,416
[banging on door]

509
00:19:50,416 --> 00:19:51,666
There they are!

510
00:19:51,666 --> 00:19:52,666
[blasting]

511
00:19:54,250 --> 00:19:56,291
Let's shut down the system!

512
00:19:59,458 --> 00:20:00,750
No!

513
00:20:02,166 --> 00:20:03,166
H'yah!

514
00:20:03,166 --> 00:20:04,333
[sparking]

515
00:20:07,666 --> 00:20:08,541
Aah!

516
00:20:08,541 --> 00:20:10,250
Wyldfyre!

517
00:20:10,250 --> 00:20:12,458
Yaah! [groaning]

518
00:20:15,166 --> 00:20:17,541
Leave her!
The portal's closing!

519
00:20:17,541 --> 00:20:19,958
You might have shattered
your goodness, but we didn't!

520
00:20:21,583 --> 00:20:22,458
Yaah!

521
00:20:22,458 --> 00:20:23,833
[Wyldfyre groans]

522
00:20:23,833 --> 00:20:25,041
Yaah!

523
00:20:25,041 --> 00:20:25,958
Hi-yaah!

524
00:20:28,125 --> 00:20:29,000
Aah!

525
00:20:31,583 --> 00:20:33,708
[grunting] They've escaped!

526
00:20:35,583 --> 00:20:36,625
[munching]

527
00:20:36,625 --> 00:20:39,375
I forgot how much
I love custard.

528
00:20:40,208 --> 00:20:41,541
[power switching off]

529
00:20:41,541 --> 00:20:43,666
[gas hissing]

530
00:20:43,666 --> 00:20:45,708
What is this, now?

531
00:20:45,708 --> 00:20:47,375
Appears... [shivering]

532
00:20:47,375 --> 00:20:50,666
...and feels unauthorized.

533
00:20:53,500 --> 00:20:55,291
Hope she'll be okay.

534
00:20:55,291 --> 00:20:58,083
We're gonna have to come back
and try to save her

535
00:20:58,083 --> 00:20:59,708
and that town.

536
00:21:10,583 --> 00:21:12,708
What is he doing?

537
00:21:12,708 --> 00:21:14,750
I have no idea.

538
00:21:18,666 --> 00:21:22,458
Yes, Master, it will be done.

539
00:21:26,208 --> 00:21:27,750
Oh, h-hey, Ras.

540
00:21:27,750 --> 00:21:30,083
The, uh, Sorceress
is settled in.

541
00:21:30,083 --> 00:21:32,291
As safe as can be, I guess.

542
00:21:32,291 --> 00:21:34,625
I do not care
about her well-being.

543
00:21:34,625 --> 00:21:36,458
She has served her purpose.

544
00:21:36,458 --> 00:21:40,000
Now... to the Underworld.

545
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:45,875
[♪♪♪]

